## Owner-scoped A2/A4 verification — 2026-10-19

A2 source checks passed: 56/56 focused schema/dispatch/route tests, strict OpenSpec 11/11, clean ESLint, independent review ACCEPT, and Code Simplifier found no further changes. A4 writer/verifier checks passed 26/26 with strict OpenSpec 11/11, independent review ACCEPT, and no Code Simplifier changes. The approved PR22 tree is main revision `876c6c4b471c5a1eb344418a249217f5b309d706`; CI `39159761994` completed build, verification, publication, and deployment. The verified source/BUILD_SHA/compiled-route/OCI/image tuple is recorded in the [SDK completion review](../../../../../nomadic-sdk/openspec/changes/add-code-mode-foundation/completion.review). This proves the A4 artifact tuple, not authenticated SystemOne response acceptance, SDK integration, or A6 semantic acceptance.

Owner decision on 2026-10-19: the full OmniRoute repository test matrix is not a gate for these A2/A4 source slices. Existing receipt `.tmp/test-matrix/20261018T231356Z/` is diagnostic only (HEAD `32b905ba0e78f3de7051a514ca69c2b61bc51029`; `summary.txt` and `SHA256SUMS`). It records unit exit 1 (Vitest 605 passed, 1 failed in `workflows-no-foreign-fork-publishers`; the assertion expects no Etcetera-specific guard while this fork has such guards, and whether either requires reconciliation is unresolved), UI 2845 passed, integration 942 passed/78 skipped, ecosystem 20 passed, protocol 2 passed, E2E web server exit 143 before tests, coverage exit 1 mirroring unit, and two ESLint unused options in `tests/unit/build/merge-official-backend-overlay.test.mjs`. These results are not a full-repository pass or a proven baseline. A separate scope audit found that the two lint bindings at lines 211–212 predate this slice: the target file has no diff from minimal-release base `484bae128d6c895ff1f106adb9afebd001e9073a`, and blame points to `0e12d43fde7` from 2026-10-04. Exclude this lint pair from A2/A4; this does not classify other matrix failures as baseline. Keep applicable repository-wide diagnosis separate; no related source repair was made here.
